## 3.1 Tombstone protection

Maintain three-layer tombstone protection.

A tombstone must not be removed or bypassed by:

- Client-side updates.
- Client-side deletes.
- Retry operations.
- Rollback operations.
- Offline synchronization.
- Reconnection.
- Parent/child collection writes.
- Unintended wildcard Security Rules.

Tombstone archival must not mean permanent deletion of the protection record.

Any archival strategy must preserve disaster-recovery and audit requirements.

## 3.2 Disaster recovery reconciliation

Preserve the eight-step DR tombstone reconciliation process from v4.2.

